  "materialNarrowings": {
    "S1": "HD5 keeps S1 literal rather than metaphorical. Kalman estimates, standards, CMB signals and product/test claims expose real representation boundaries, but many physical-device trajectories are N/A. DNA and laser cases narrow any reading that predicts one uniquely privileged representation must precede productive convergence.",
    "S2": "Polio/Cutter, thalidomide, semiconductor yield and staged Apollo tests make evaluator failure modes concrete. Independent verification can be a chain of different evaluators across lifecycle phases rather than one final test.",
    "S3": "The applicability-scope narrowing from HD1 strengthens: a result can be real within one service/manufacturing/world regime while opening a new scale, geography or lifecycle frontier. Platform/service claims require materially different conditions inside the declared claim scope, not arbitrary universality.",
    "S4": "Method choice remains regime-conditioned but can settle locally for long periods: Toyota pull, LOR, reactor routes, vaccine routes and semiconductor processes are conditioned choices, not evidence that constant switching is good.",
    "S5": "S5 is directly applicable where a compact durable representation is the technical object—Kalman state, long-lived environmental record, standards or reusable software—but remains N/A for most physical inventions. It is not promoted as a universal historical law.",
    "S6": "Additional complexity can be justified by whole-system value even when it looks locally costly: LOR rendezvous, planar process control, container standards and parallel vaccine/reactor routes. Repayment must bind objective, world boundary and time horizon.",
    "S7": "Metaproductivity remains separable from current performance. Mohole, Brabazon and nuclear-aircraft failures can preserve option value; polio life-saving current value need not be the same as future research-capacity value.",
    "S8": "HD5 repeatedly exposes phase-specific prediction errors: manufacturing yield, vaccine lot safety, plate-motion predictions, numerical-weather error, Apollo integration and satellite service availability. Model correction binds realized consequence at the relevant phase.",
    "S9": "Technical success does not settle admissibility in vaccine manufacture, drug regulation, dialysis allocation, nuclear power, Apollo risk or infrastructure displacement. Authority and consequence boundaries remain domain-specific.",
    "S10": "Platform/service-era trajectories strongly reject one scalar: transistor action versus yield, vaccine efficacy versus lot safety, launcher performance versus mission closure, crop yield versus input/environmental burden, and highway throughput versus social cost diverge."
  },
